# This repository has `core.autocrlf=true`, so git rewrites text files to CRLF in the working tree on
# every checkout, stash pop and branch switch. That is fine almost everywhere. It is not fine for the
# .mjs scripts, which are imported directly by vitest fitness tests:
#
#   apps/api/src/governed-routes.fitness.test.ts  ->  apps/api/scripts/route-permission-audit.mjs
#   apps/api/src/finance-authority.fitness.test.ts       (same script)
#
# When one of those files comes back with CRLF, vitest fails to load it with
#
#     SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token
#
# pointing at the IMPORTING test file, while `node --check` parses the same file without complaint —
# the transform chokes on a `#!` shebang line terminated by CRLF. Nothing in the message says "line
# endings", and it cost two wrong diagnoses before the cause was found, so it is pinned here.
#
# Deliberately narrow. A repo-wide `* text=auto eol=lf` would rewrite every file in the working tree
# on the next checkout, which is a much larger change than this problem needs.
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.cjs   text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf

# Never rewrite these at all.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.xls   binary
*.docx  binary
*.zip   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
